{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/123055","id":4406657217,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABBqhAwQ","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123055","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123055.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123055.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123055","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/123055/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/123055/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123055/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/0bc75b87ec4c3cf56407f9163929f7ba3549c51a","number":123055,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Use copy_from to overwrite resources in cache","user":{"login":"demolke","id":153469044,"node_id":"U_kgDOCSXAdA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/153469044?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/demolke","html_url":"https://github.com/demolke","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/demolke/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/demolke/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/demolke/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/demolke/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/demolke/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/demolke/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/demolke/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/demolke/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/demolke/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"When editing resources externally, reimport will run, process them and then ResourceBinaryLoader will be called with CACHE_MODE_REPLACE. It will take the existing resource from cache, perform reset_state, then load the stored properties from the file.\r\n\r\nThe problem is that this does not handle well properties which are no longer defined by the new resource. They do not get overwritten and stay around.\r\n\r\nI think this was introduced by https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/97362 / https://github.com/godotengine/godot/commit/abf9d245208542ccf883f6b61f0d3be486dc9447. Previously we would get new ids for resources on re-import, so the caching would not find them and they would not get re-used. But once the hashing became deterministic, we find the resource and not clear all of it's properties.\r\n\r\nI first had an attempt to fix it [here](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120380), but that was not the right approach. I think doing it the same way as https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/2c089e9bf0b8712d0bc444c2ceaf9c543ed9c777/core/io/resource_loader.cpp#L591 is probably the way to go.\r\n\r\nAI disclosure - I used it to help me write the test. I wrote the original test for a material property and then AI came up with the perturb idea to test all the properties, which I though was neat. I would say it's like 50:50.\r\n\r\n## What problem(s) does this PR solve?\r\n\r\n- Closes #104937\r\n- Closes #119131\r\n- Closes #105474\r\n\r\n## Additional information\r\n\r\nBefore and after video\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/681c70ff-a0c7-45a7-a180-43d335088272\r\n\r\n[project](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/29065482/material.zip)","labels":[{"id":73330064,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2NA==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/bug","name":"bug","description":"","color":"ff6055","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":890310502,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw4OTAzMTA1MDI=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:import","name":"topic:import","description":"","c